      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: clarify SQLite version error message to prevent user confusion",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users seeing the SQLite version error would be confused by the message \"3.44.6+\" and think it meant \"3.44.6 and above\", when in fact only the 3.44.x series received the WAL-reset bug fix. This led to confusion when versions like 3.46.1 were rejected despite being numerically higher than 3.44.6.\n\nThe issue was reported in #108273 where a user with Node 24.18.0 (SQLite 3.46.1) thought their version should be accepted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe error message has been clarified to explicitly state \"3.44.6+ in the 3.44.x series\" and \"3.50.7+ in the 3.50.x series\" instead of just \"3.44.6+ or 3.50.7+\". This matches the SQLite team's actual fix announcement which only backported the WAL-reset bug fix to specific minor version series (3.44.x and 3.50.x), plus the main fix in 3.51.3+.\n\nThe code logic remains unchanged - this is purely a clarity improvement to the error message.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who encounter the SQLite version check error will now immediately understand why their version is not accepted, without needing to research SQLite version numbering or the WAL-reset bug fix history. The message now clearly explains that only specific version series received the fix.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- All existing tests pass: 22 tests in `src/infra/node-sqlite.test.ts`\n- Build succeeds: `pnpm build` completed successfully\n- Type checking passes: `pnpm tsgo:core` has no errors\n- The error message now explicitly states which version series are safe:\n  - \"3.44.6+ in the 3.44.x series\"\n  - \"3.50.7+ in the 3.50.x series\"\n  - \"3.51.3+\"\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Existing test suite validates the version checking logic\n- No new tests needed since this is purely an error message clarification\n- Tests already cover the rejection of versions like 3.46.1\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] No functional behavior change - only error message text modified\n- [x] No API changes\n- [x] No config/schema changes\n- [x] No migration needed\n- [x] Backward compatible - clearer error messages benefit all users\n\n## Current review state\n\nReady for review.\n\n---\n\n🤖 AI-assisted: This PR was developed with AI assistance (co-mind)",
